---
import { BOOK_A_CALL_PATH } from '../../consts';

// CRM is a supporting capability (not a standalone service), presented on the
// AI for Entrepreneurs page as one place AI and automation pay off.
const capabilities = [
  {
    title: 'CRM setup and cleanup',
    text: 'Pipelines, fields, and lead stages that match how you actually sell, plus cleanup of duplicate or outdated contacts so your data is worth automating.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Lead capture that lands in one place',
    text: 'Website forms, ad leads, and booking requests flow straight into your CRM with their source attached, so no inquiry sits forgotten in an inbox.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Email marketing automation',
    text: 'Welcome, nurture, and follow-up sequences that send the right message at the right time and stop when a lead replies or books a call.',
  },
  {
    title: 'AI-assisted follow-up',
    text: 'AI that drafts personalized follow-ups, summarizes lead activity, and flags the contacts most ready for a conversation, with you approving what goes out.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section crm" aria-labelledby="crm-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="crm-title">CRM and email automation that follows up for you</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      AI is only as useful as the systems it plugs into. For most small businesses, that's the CRM, where leads arrive,
      follow-ups get scheduled, and opportunities quietly slip away when nobody has time. I bring hands-on CRM and
      marketing automation experience to make that system work on its own, with AI handling the repetitive parts.
    </p>

    <ul class="capabilities" role="list">
      {
        capabilities.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p class="platforms placeholder-note">[REPLACE: CRM and email platforms you work with, e.g. the tools you're certified in]</p>

    <p>
      Once your CRM is set up, it can feed a <a href="/marketing-analytics-and-dashboards">custom marketing performance dashboard</a> so you can see which channels bring in leads that turn into customers.
    </p>

    <a class="btn btn-primary" href={BOOK_A_CALL_PATH}>Talk through your CRM and follow-up process</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .crm {
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 65ch;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .capabilities {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .capabilities {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-5);
    }
  }

  .capabilities li {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .capabilities p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .platforms {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }
</style>
